# Default build context exclusions.
#
# WARNING: excluding a path here makes a COPY of that path fail with
# "not found" in any Dockerfile using this context, and the error never
# mentions .dockerignore. Three builds have broken this way already
# (revok.yaml, examples/, tests/), so record the coupling below.
#
# Which builds depend on the exceptions in this file:
#   examples/ + !examples/subscription_demo/{server,agent,database,demo_state}.py
#       -> examples/subscription_demo/Dockerfile.api
#   examples/ + !examples/subscription_demo/revok.yaml
#       -> examples/subscription_demo/Dockerfile.revok
#
# Builds that need paths this file excludes use their own ignore file, since
# Docker prefers <dockerfile-name>.dockerignore over this one:
#   Dockerfile.falkordblite-tests -> Dockerfile.falkordblite-tests.dockerignore
#   Dockerfile.redis-tests        -> Dockerfile.redis-tests.dockerignore
# Both re-include tests/, which stays excluded here to keep production
# images lean. Adding an exclusion here means updating those files too.
.git
.venv
__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
examples/
# Re-include demo source files needed by Dockerfile.api build
!examples/subscription_demo/server.py
!examples/subscription_demo/agent.py
!examples/subscription_demo/database.py
!examples/subscription_demo/demo_state.py
# Re-include demo config needed by Dockerfile.revok build
!examples/subscription_demo/revok.yaml
tests/
*.md
.gitignore
TASKS.md
.env*
*.log*
coverage/
